Deliberately not an open-source licence, for the same reason as Farewatch: this
was built as a side project with the intention that it might eventually earn
money, and a permissive licence would let anyone stand up a competing service
from the same code. If that stops being the goal, MIT is a one-file change.

Data used at runtime is not covered by this notice and remains subject to its
own terms:

  * Steam store and review data from store.steampowered.com, property of Valve.
  * Ownership and tag data from steamspy.com.

Greenlight reads both through their public endpoints, caches locally, and
republishes neither.
